# ── Public-repo boundary (SPEC: Security & Privacy) — never commit ──────────
# Patterns are anchored where needed: ziggurat/data/ is the (public) ingestion
# package; only the top-level intel/ and data/ trees are league-private.
/intel/
/data/
# A SEPARATOR CLASS, not a trailing wildcard (item 3.2c). End-anchored `*.sqlite`
# matched neither a backup named ziggurat.sqlite.bak-v7 nor ziggurat.sqlite.gz,
# and repo_guard.py was anchored the same way — so a 43 MB file of league-private
# data cleared TWO of the three enforcement points Rule 5 names. But a bare
# `*.sqlite*` over-matches in the other direction and would swallow a source file
# named foo.sqliteish.py, so the suffix must begin with `.` or `-`.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite.*
*.sqlite3.*
*.sqlite-*
*.sqlite3-*
.env
.env.*
.env-*
# direnv; routinely holds `export SECRET=...`. Named exactly, not `.env*`, which
# would be the same over-matching mistake the sqlite block above documents.
.envrc

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage*
htmlcov/

# ── Local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store
